== Building

This will build the default output for your _<%= info["fullName"] %>_.

 $ nix-build --argstr device <%= info["identifier"] %> -A outputs.default

=== Installation

Before Mobile NixOS can be installed on your _<%= info["fullName"] %>_
you will first need to install the "lk2nd" second-stage
bootloader. This is flashed to the `boot` partition in place of an
Android-style boot image, and when started it will look across
all the other partitions for an extlinux-style boot partition to
continue booting.

 $ nix-build --argstr device <%= info["identifier"] %> -A outputs.default
 $ fastboot flash boot result/lk2nd.img

lk2nd also implements the Android fastboot protocol. If you are
already booted to the lk2nd screen and want to upgrade to a newer
lk2nd, then you should flash to `lk2nd` instead of `boot`

 $ nix-build --argstr device <%= info["identifier"] %> -A outputs.default
 $ fastboot flash lk2nd result/lk2nd.img
